From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: A move of the pointer made for a moved window merges with the others.

Every window whose rectangle changes makes wineserver queue a WM_MOUSEMOVE
at the pointer (update_cursor_pos), and it could not be merged. Explorer
lays out a dozen child windows at each step of a resize: each move of the
pointer then came after one of those and stayed a message of its own, and
the size loop went through every position the pointer had passed, behind
it more the further it was dragged (380 px and half a second, measured).
Windows makes that move once, when the queue is read; merged, the queue
holds one move, at the pointer's last position.
---
diff --git a/server/queue.c b/server/queue.c
--- a/server/queue.c
+++ b/server/queue.c
@@ -585,6 +585,11 @@
     msg->msg = WM_MOUSEMOVE;
     msg->x   = x;
     msg->y   = y;
+    /* Windows makes such a move once, when the queue is read: queued for
+     * every window moved, unmerged, it kept the pointer's own moves apart,
+     * and a window whose children are laid out at each step of a resize
+     * (Explorer) went through every position the pointer had passed */
+    msg->mergeable = true;
     queue_hardware_message( desktop, msg, 1 );
 }
 
